<title>UK: Cable &amp; Wireless up as Laing repeats &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>Cable &amp; Wireless up as Laing repeats &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cable and Wireless rose on Monday after analysts at Credit Lyonnais Laing repeated a &quot;buy&quot; recommmendation on the stock, traders said.</p>
<p>Cable and Wireless shares were 8-1/2p higher at 518p 1015 GMT.  </p>
<p>Analyst Steve Scruton said he expected C&amp;W to join the Global One joint venture between Deutsche Telekom AG, France Telecom and Sprint Corp</p>
<p>&quot;This deal should help to bring the shares up towards our 5.80 stg target price,&quot; Scruton said.</p>
<p>-- Simon Gardner, London Newsroom + 44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
